# integration.suite — the full-integration flows that run in throwaway
# containers: every node in its own Docker container on one network.
#
# Run it with `--docker` on a host with a Docker engine; without --docker it
# runs in local worlds. Every test here is Docker-eligible: no VM ops, and
# nothing that reaches the host beyond the session view, host_ip (an app or
# authority the test serves, `host_listener`) and lib/nodefs.py. The planner
# refuses a test that is not.
#
# The order is a preference among siblings; the planner computes the run
# order from each test's `after`. expel-node is listed before hold-purge so
# that hold-purge, which also ends a world, forks instead of expel-node.
smoke
claim-window
token-less-setup
signer-app
admission-policies
bootstrap-user-software-key
adopt-node
blueprints-two-node
apphost-origin
